{:edb/db-before-t 1563 :edb/db-after-t 1564 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534876 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:49:42.984Z" 13194139534876 true] [17592186124314 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{4} + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{2} = \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{3}$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." 13194139534876 false] [17592186124314 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{4} + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{2} = \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{3},$ find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." 13194139534876 true] [17592186124314 1145 "To find the $z$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((0 - 2)^{2})/(4) + ((0 - 2)^{2})/(2) &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n\\frac{4}{4} + \\frac{4}{2} &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n1 + 2 &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n3 &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n9 &= (z + 1)^{2} \\\\\nz + 1 &= ± 3 \\\\\nz &= -1 ± 3 \\\\\nz &= -4, 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2)$." 13194139534876 false] [17592186124314 1145 "To find the $z$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{4}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 1+2 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 9 & =(z+1)^{2} \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-4,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186124315 1100 "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 +  4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\: ?$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186124315 1100 "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 + 4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\:$?" 13194139534876 false] [17592186124315 1145 "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x^{2} + 4 \\cdot 0^{2} &= 12(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\n3x^{2} &= 12(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} &= 4(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\n± x &= 2(z + 3) \\\\\n± \\frac{x}{2} &= z + 3 \\\\\nz &= ± \\frac{x}{2} - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations\n\n$$\nz = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3\n$$" 13194139534876 false] [17592186124315 1145 "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4\\cdot {0}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(z+3)^{2} \\\\ \\pm x & =2(z+3) \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x}{2} & =z+3 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{x}{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3.$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316760 13194139534876 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316788 13194139534876 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316795 13194139534876 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316767 13194139534876 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316774 13194139534876 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316781 13194139534876 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316802 13194139534876 true] [17592186124809 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534876 true] [17592186124809 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = (z - 4)^{2}$?" 13194139534876 false] [17592186124809 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=(z-4)^{2}\\,?$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186124809 1145 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{y}{2} & =z-4 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4.$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186125154 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534876 true] [17592186125154 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $((x - 2)^{2})/(2) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(4) = (z + 3)^{2}$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139534876 false] [17592186125154 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=(z+3)^{2},$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139534876 true] [17592186125154 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{4} & =(0+3)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{4}{4} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+1 & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2} & =8 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-2,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186125155 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534876 true] [17592186125155 1100 "Find the center of the elliptic cone $2(x + 2)^{2} + 3(y - 1)^{2} = z^{2}$." 13194139534876 false] [17592186125155 1100 "Find the center of the elliptic cone $2(x+2)^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186125155 1145 "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+2)^{2}+3(y-1)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{1/2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1/3} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{1/2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1/3} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(-2,1,0).$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316761 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1089 "q-176833" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x+8)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3}=\\frac{(z-7)^{2}}{7},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1113 #uuid "476b5ba6-7557-5084-9691-646b1cb8f507" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316760 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+8)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =\\frac{(0-7)^{2}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{64}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =\\frac{49}{7} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{6} & =7 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =3 \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y+5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-5\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-8,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0).$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316762 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316763 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316764 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316765 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316766 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1041 "selection" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316764 13194139534876 true] [17592186316761 1110 #uuid "22a66afc-c3e6-5b03-b787-381fe0c34aba" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316762 1034 "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316762 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534876 true] [17592186316762 1111 #uuid "1dde02e1-716e-52ec-aff6-2776c21d7fa7" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316763 1034 "$(0,-2,0)$ only" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316763 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534876 true] [17592186316763 1111 #uuid "8231b6c6-cfa5-5a9f-84b4-4fe2c7413ced" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316764 1034 "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0)$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316764 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534876 true] [17592186316764 1111 #uuid "b246ed0d-76b5-5d1b-b38f-3a23929cd24b" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316765 1034 "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,7,0)$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534876 true] [17592186316765 1111 #uuid "0125cce2-e928-5bca-85fb-b39ef96df5a7" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316766 1034 "$(0,-8,0)$ only" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534876 true] [17592186316766 1111 #uuid "eb2cb3c5-4613-57cb-a342-dfcc82ef64e6" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316768 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1089 "q-35266" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1100 "Given that the trace of the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}={z}^{2}$ and the $xz$-plane are two lines, what is the intersection point of these lines?" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1113 #uuid "8cf1e2a7-da38-57ea-b1de-04392dc7110c" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316767 1145 "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x-1}{2} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\frac{x-1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{1-x}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the point of intersection of both lines, we equate the right-hand sides. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =1-x \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ in the equation of the first line and solving for $z,$ we obtain $z=\\frac{1-1}{2}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(1,0,0).$" 13194139534876 true] [17592186316768 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316769 13194139534876 true] [17592186316768 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316770 13194139534876 true] [17592186316768 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316771 13194139534876 true] [17592186316